-- Next definitions (2026-11-12, "P2.6e from p26-wip"; latest, supersedes P2.6d and P2.6e above).
-- Done and checked in experiments/nbe/p26-wip.cub (a working copy of this file with P1's families
-- removed; "364 passed, 0 failed"): s-path in TyShape (TyE's clause PathS/PathE written out,
-- sem-path by refl); P2.6d entire: Jdg over CCtx, the rule data and projections above, lam-dom/
-- lam-ctx/lam-body, plam-line/plam-body, carry, papp-mean (path application at f, carried along
-- papp-deg), NN (nvar … npair, nplam, npapp with isTrue (dnf-canon f), isTrue (dnf-nonconst f), Y and
-- PathM (papp-mean Γ a f P) Y), Der likewise (dpapp without the non-constancy field), TCode, teval,
-- embed; P2.6e begun: cube-const, dcube-const, CMap, cmap-cube, cmap-d, SubF, sub-base, Sub,
-- sub-carried, sub-pull, subM; item (3) below: fmap-const, fmap-cmap, pull-fmap, subM-fmap.
-- Finding (2026-11-12, theoretical; it extends the substitutions of the finding above): fund
-- (dplam) must give CompS a at every later world and every canonical form f (the PathP clause), and
-- computability is not stable under substituting a constant for a world's dimension (the reason
-- worlds exclude it), so it is fund on the body at a substitution sending the body's dimension to f.
-- So a substitution's dimension part is a map of the cube category given, as in CCHM, by an interval
-- form over Δ's skeleton for each dimension of Γ's (CMap: its action is cube-const, then papp-cube at
-- each form, newest innermost), not only a composite of degeneracies; a world's forms are distinct
-- variables in order.
-- (2026-11-12, later) Done since, checked in p26-wip ("455 passed, 0 failed", no cache): (1) entire:
-- lit-r/conj-r/dnf-r (a structural map of variables), MonoW, dnf-canon-r (dnf-norm commutes with a
-- monotone injection, through every operation), dnf-nonconst-r; OPE as closed data (wdone, wskip e,
-- wkeep e; ope-src, ope-tgt; indexed by the two skeletons, its wdone clauses carry fording's
-- transports, which do not reduce), ope-var, ope-mono, dnf-ren, canon-ren, nonconst-ren. (4) on
-- cubes: ope-cube (skip-cube, keep-cube), ope-nat, diag-sk at a successor (diag-ty-s, diag-dim-s),
-- diag-nat, diag-ren, papp-ren (through papp-lit/conj-from/conj/dnf-from with offsets, RenAt). (2) on
-- cubes: cmap-of sk' sk r (dimension k to the variable r k), cmap-skip (weakening by a type is the
-- same cube, by a dimension the degenerate one), cmap-keep, cmap-id, cmap-ope (= ope-cube). Tickets
-- t53, t54 (elaborator; neither workaround is in use).
-- (2026-11-12, latest) Done since, checked in p26-wip ("494 passed, 0 failed", no cache): (2d) entire:
-- pcat-d/psym-d (a path over a composite of base paths, by the filler of the base pcat), reidx-comp,
-- reidx-id, cube-comp2-d; skip-d, keep-d, ope-cube-d, ope-nat-d; diag-ty-s-d, diag-dim-s-d,
-- diag-nat-d, skip-diag-d, keep-diag-d, diag-ren-d; const-map-d, skip-const-d, papp-var-d,
-- cmap-skip-d, cmap-keep-d, cmap-id-d, cmap-ope-d (each a PathP over its law on the base). (2s) in
-- part: sub-id, sub-wk (by a type), sub-dwk (by a dimension), with dmap-map, dmap-fst; papp-nat
-- (path application natural in the base, through papp-lit-nat … papp-dnf-from-nat), cmap-nat;
-- sub-form (σ extended by a form g over Δ for Γ's new dimension: Sub Δ (dext Γ); its path is
-- cmap-nat at the degeneracy, papp-deg, then σ's own).
-- Settled (2026-11-12, by the coordinator, checked): the evaluator identifies interval expressions up
-- to the De Morgan laws judgmentally; each of these checks by refl: Path (x ≡ y) (λ i → p (i ∨ (i ∧
-- i))) p; Path (x ≡ y) (λ i → p (~ (~ i))) p; Path (y ≡ x) (λ i → p (~ (i ∧ i))) (λ i → p (~ i));
-- Path (x ≡ y) (λ i → p (i ∨ (i ∧ (~ i)))) p. So (4d)'s first step is answered: path application is a
-- homomorphism for meet, join and negation by refl on lines, and by induction on n on cubes.
-- Decision (2026-11-12, theoretical): a world into Δ is stated over fst Δ' and fst Δ directly, not as
-- an OPE w with an equation ope-tgt w ≡ fst Δ. Δ is a variable context in CompS's Kripke clause, so
-- such an equation is a path between a computed skeleton and a variable one, and transports of cubes
-- along it do not reduce (the reason OPE is closed data, above); cmap-of (fst Δ') (fst Δ) r needs no
-- equation. A world Δ' → Δ: r : Word → Word with MonoW r (so canon-ren's argument applies: dnf-r r
-- keeps canonicity, nonconst-ren non-constancy) sending each dimension index of fst Δ to a dimension
-- index of fst Δ' (so a renamed cpapp's form names dimensions); the Sub (cmap-of (fst Δ') (fst Δ) r ,
-- S , path); and P1's Ren over cubes for term variables (each v : VarP (fst Δ) to a v' : VarP (fst
-- Δ') with var-word and a PathM from subM of varCube Δ v to varCube Δ' v'). Weakening by a type is
-- r = succ (sub-wk), by a dimension likewise (sub-dwk), keeping is w-keep r, composition is r2 ∘ r1.
-- ren-nn at npapp needs subM along the world of papp-mean at f to be papp-mean at dnf-r r f of subM:
-- this is subM-papp (4d) at cmap-of r, with dnf-sub (cmap-of r) f ≡ dnf-r r f for canonical f and
-- monotone r (dnf-canon-r's argument). The OPE forms of (1), (4), (2d) (ope-cube, papp-ren, cmap-ope
-- and their dependent forms) are the case r = ope-var w with matching skeletons.
-- Remaining, in order (each a closed statement):
--   (2s) the rest: extension by a cube of values, sub-ext Δ Γ a Y f M σ V : Sub Δ (extM Γ a Y f M),
--       V a cube over the total of Q = dcube-pull of sub-carried σ M along σ's S (fibre (p : SubF) ×
--       FbE (fst Γ) Y (fst p)) with fibre ρ' ↦ El a (f (fst p) e (snd p ρ')); S' = dcube-pull of V
--       at ((γ , f γ e) , λ ρ' → (em ρ' , v ρ')); its path: cmap-dmap (cmap-cube of a dcube-map is
--       dcube-map over cmap-cube and cmap-d, through papp-dmap: papp-cube of a dcube-map is dcube-map
--       of papp-cube and papp-cube-d, by papp-nat's recursion; dmap-const-cube at lnil), the filler
--       of sub-carried's carry, map-pull (dcube-map out of a dcube-pull along a pairing is dcube-map
--       over the pushed base), dmap-map, and dcube-map-of. Worlds as decided above (World, world-sub,
--       world-wk, world-dwk, world-keep, world-comp).
--   (4d) papp-ren-d (papp-cube-d at dnf-ren w f over papp-ren, by papp-ren's recursion with
--       diag-ren-d and ope-nat-d), then subM-papp: dnf-sub σ f replaces a literal (k , b) by σ's
--       form for k (dnf-neg of it when b is false), a conjunction by dnf-meet, a disjunction by
--       dnf-join; by the recursion of papp-cube, a literal by the induction on sk that cmap-cube's
--       newest form is snd σ, the connections by the De Morgan laws holding judgmentally (above);
--       then dnf-sub (cmap-of r) f ≡ dnf-r r f (f canonical, r monotone), and papp-mean along a
--       world (ren-nn at npapp).
--   (5) subM-comp for worlds: comp-ren.
--   (6) ren-nn (along worlds, transported along (3), (4d)); CompS by recursion on the shape with the
--       PathP clause; comp-ren; rr; CompEnv over a substitution; fund; reflect-env; normalize;
--       reifySound and normalize-sound by refl; the swap into this file in place of P1's families;
--       experiments/nbe/examples.cub rewritten over the new families (P1's examples with the same
--       normal forms, ⟨i⟩ b, the η-long path variable, p @ 0).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- types: shapes and their semantic types
-- (2026-11-12, step 1) A type of shape s over environments G is a map from G into Sem s, the semantic
-- types of shape s; its meaning at ρ is El s (T ρ). Sem and El are defined together by recursion on
-- the closed shape (one pair, TyE, since mutual definitions by clauses are not available), so El of
-- an open semantic type computes by its shape's clause. Levels are closed everywhere (the finding at
-- the head): El s is
-- in Type (the stratum of P1's shapes; P6 adds the stratum whose meanings are in Type 1), Sem s and
-- environments are in Type 1, so a semantic type may contain a Type (the universe's El, P6) and an
-- environment may contain a type, with nothing lifted.
data TyShape = s-bool | s-pi (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape) | s-sig (a : TyShape) (b : TyShape)
-- the semantic Bool type: nothing; One1 is a type at level 1 with the one value `one`
data One1 = one1 (pad : Type → Type)
one : One1
one = one1 (λ X → X)
TyU : Type 2
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
TyU = (uM : Type 1) × (uM → Type)
-- binders hatted (Â D̂ x̂) because of t46 (telescope instantiation captures names)
TyE : TyShape → TyU
TyE s-bool = (One1 , λ D̂ → Bool)
TyE (s-pi a b) =
  ((Â : fst (TyE a)) × (snd (TyE a) Â → fst (TyE b)) ,
   λ D̂ → (x̂ : snd (TyE a) (fst D̂)) → snd (TyE b) (snd D̂ x̂))
TyE (s-sig a b) =
  ((Â : fst (TyE a)) × (snd (TyE a) Â → fst (TyE b)) ,
   λ D̂ → (x̂ : snd (TyE a) (fst D̂)) × snd (TyE b) (snd D̂ x̂))
Sem : TyShape → Type 1
Sem s = fst (TyE s)
El : (s : TyShape) → Sem s → Type
El s = snd (TyE s)
-- the semantic types of Π and Σ: a domain and a family over it (the same for both)
Fam : TyShape → TyShape → Type 1
Fam a b = (A : Sem a) × (El a A → Sem b)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- types over a context's environments
-- a type over environments G: a shape and a map into its semantic types; its meaning; pulling back
-- along f : H → G is composition (definitional)
PTy : Type 1 → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
PTy G = (ps : TyShape) × (G → Sem ps)
ElP : (G : Type 1) → PTy G → G → Type
ElP G A ρ = El (fst A) (snd A ρ)
pull : (G H : Type 1) → (H → G) → PTy G → PTy H
pull G H f A = (fst A , λ h → snd A (f h))
-- the domain of a Π (or Σ) type over G, and its codomain over G extended by the domain
dom : (G : Type 1) (a b : TyShape) (T : G → Fam a b) → PTy G
dom G a b T = (a , λ ρ → fst (T ρ))
cod : (G : Type 1) (a b : TyShape) (T : G → Fam a b) → PTy ((ρ : G) × ElP G (dom G a b T) ρ)
cod G a b T = (b , λ p → snd (T (fst p)) (snd p))
-- the meanings are the language's own Π and Σ (definitionally)
pi-meaning : (G : Type 1) (a b : TyShape) (T : G → Fam a b) (ρ : G) →
  Path Type (ElP G (s-pi a b , T) ρ) ((x : ElP G (dom G a b T) ρ) → ElP ((ρ : G) × ElP G (dom G a b T) ρ) (cod G a b T) (ρ , x))
pi-meaning G a b T ρ = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- contexts
-- a context over a skeleton (its entries' shapes, closed data): the entries' types and the type of
-- its environments, by recursion on the skeleton; environments are in Type 1 (the empty one is One1)
-- (P2.2, 2026-11-12) A skeleton's entries are types' shapes or dimensions, newest first. A dimension
-- contributes nothing to a vertex's environment (its direction is the cube's, P2.6); codes count it
-- among the de Bruijn indices.
data Entry = e-ty (s : TyShape) | e-dim
dims : Lst Entry → Nat
dims lnil = zero
dims (lcons (e-ty s) sk) = dims sk
dims (lcons e-dim sk) = suc (dims sk)
CtxU : Type 2
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
CtxU = (uM : Type 1) × (uM → Type 1)
CtxE : Lst Entry → CtxU
CtxE lnil = (One1 , λ γ → One1)
CtxE (lcons e-dim sk) = CtxE sk
CtxE (lcons (e-ty s) sk) =
  ((γ : fst (CtxE sk)) × (snd (CtxE sk) γ → Sem s) ,
   λ p → (ρ : snd (CtxE sk) (fst p)) × El s (snd p ρ))
Ctx : Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Ctx = (csk : Lst Entry) × fst (CtxE csk)
Env : Ctx → Type 1
Env Γ = snd (CtxE (fst Γ)) (snd Γ)
emp : Ctx
emp = (lnil , one)
-- Γ extended by a type over its environments
ext : (Γ : Ctx) → PTy (Env Γ) → Ctx
ext Γ A = (lcons (e-ty (fst A)) (fst Γ) , (snd Γ , snd A))
ext-env : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → Path (Type 1) (Env (ext Γ A)) ((ρ : Env Γ) × ElP (Env Γ) A ρ)
ext-env Γ A = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- variables
-- the dependent eliminator of Bool, for the meanings of case
bool-elim : (P : Bool → Type) → P true → P false → (b : Bool) → P b
bool-elim P t f true = t
bool-elim P t f false = f
-- the four parts every judgment here is indexed by: a context, a type over its environments, a raw
-- code and the code's meaning (the indices are one Σ: a family's indices may not depend on each other)
Jdg : Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Jdg = (jΓ : Ctx) × (jA : PTy (Env jΓ)) × Code × ((jρ : Env jΓ) → ElP (Env jΓ) jA jρ)
-- the variable n of Γ, of type A, with meaning v (a projection out of the environment), by recursion
-- on the skeleton (2026-11-12: an indexed family of variables cannot be matched inside an extended
-- context, since the elaborator does not unify the computed index ext Γ A with a constructor's (t47); a
-- type computed on the closed skeleton is matched as a sum, and its equations are explicit paths)
-- a type over Γ weakened to Γ extended by B
wk : (Γ : Ctx) (B : PTy (Env Γ)) → PTy (Env Γ) → PTy (Env (ext Γ B))
wk Γ B A = pull (Env Γ) (Env (ext Γ B)) (λ ρ → fst ρ) A
data Sum1 (A : Type 1) (B : Type 1) = inl1 (a : A) | inr1 (b : B)
Empty1 : Type 1
Empty1 = Empty × One1
VIx : Type 1 → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
VIx G = (vA : PTy G) × Word × ((vρ : G) → ElP G vA vρ)
-- PathP (λ i → …), not Path, and refl at an explicit level, wherever the type is an application at
-- Type 1: t50
VarT : (sk : Lst Entry) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) → VIx (Env (sk , γ)) → Type 1
VarT lnil γ X = Empty1
-- past a dimension: a variable of the skeleton below, one index further, its type and meaning unchanged
VarT (lcons e-dim sk) γ X =
  (Y : VIx (Env (sk , γ))) × VarT sk γ Y × PathP (λ i → VIx (Env (sk , γ))) X (fst Y , %wsucc (fst (snd Y)) , snd (snd Y))
VarT (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ X =
  Sum1 (PathP (λ i → VIx (Env (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ))) X (wk (sk , fst γ) (s , snd γ) (s , snd γ) , #0 , λ ρ → snd ρ))
       ((Y : VIx (Env (sk , fst γ))) × VarT sk (fst γ) Y ×
        PathP (λ i → VIx (Env (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ))) X (wk (sk , fst γ) (s , snd γ) (fst Y) , %wsucc (fst (snd Y)) , λ ρ → snd (snd Y) (fst ρ)))
Var : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (n : Word) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) → Type 1
Var Γ A n v = VarT (fst Γ) (snd Γ) (A , n , v)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- neutral and normal forms
-- one family for both (mutual data types are not available), the kind in the index. η-long: a
-- neutral is normal only at Bool. The codes are the ones the language's (code t) writes: Bool is
-- data #0, true and false its constructors #0 and #1, case on it ccase #0 with the two branches.
-- A Bool type is (s-bool , B) for any B : G → One1 (One1 has no η), so the Bool rules take any B.
data NK = k-ne | k-nf
-- substituting a meaning for the last variable
at-last : (G : Type 1) (A : PTy G) (va : (ρ : G) → ElP G A ρ) → PTy ((ρ : G) × ElP G A ρ) → PTy G
at-last G A va B = pull ((ρ : G) × ElP G A ρ) G (λ ρ → (ρ , va ρ)) B
c-true : Code
c-true = ccon #0 #0 lnil lnil
c-false : Code
c-false = ccon #0 #1 lnil lnil
c-case : Code → Code → Code → Code
c-case t f x = ccase #0 (lcons t (lcons f lnil)) x
-- constructor binders subscripted ₀: t46
data NN : (KJ : NK × Jdg) → Type 1 where
  nvar : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (A₀ : PTy (Env Γ₀)) (n₀ : Word) (v₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) A₀ ρ₀) →
    Var Γ₀ A₀ n₀ v₀ → NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , A₀ , cvar n₀ , v₀))
  napp : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (f₀ : Code) (vf₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀)
    (c₀ : Code) (va₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) , f₀ , vf₀)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c₀ , va₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) va₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , capp f₀ c₀ , λ ρ₀ → vf₀ ρ₀ (va₀ ρ₀)))
  nfst : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (p₀ : Code) (vp₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , p₀ , vp₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , cfst p₀ , λ ρ₀ → fst (vp₀ ρ₀)))
  nsnd : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (p₀ : Code) (vp₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , p₀ , vp₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) (λ ρ₀ → fst (vp₀ ρ₀)) (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , csnd p₀ , λ ρ₀ → snd (vp₀ ρ₀)))
  ncase : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) (P₀ : PTy (Env (ext Γ₀ (s-bool , B₀)))) (x₀ : Code) (vx₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → Bool)
    (t₀ : Code) (vt₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → true) P₀) ρ₀)
    (f₀ : Code) (vf₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → false) P₀) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , x₀ , vx₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → true) P₀ , t₀ , vt₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → false) P₀ , f₀ , vf₀)) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) vx₀ P₀ , c-case t₀ f₀ x₀ ,
                λ ρ₀ → bool-elim (λ b₀ → ElP (Env (ext Γ₀ (s-bool , B₀))) P₀ (ρ₀ , b₀)) (vt₀ ρ₀) (vf₀ ρ₀) (vx₀ ρ₀)))
  nne : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) (x₀ : Code) (vx₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → Bool) →
    NN (k-ne , (Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , x₀ , vx₀)) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , x₀ , vx₀))
  ntrue : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , c-true , λ ρ₀ → true))
  nfalse : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) → NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , c-false , λ ρ₀ → false))
  nlam : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (c₀ : Code) (vb₀ : (ρ₀ : Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) → ElP (Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-nf , (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c₀ , vb₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) , clam c₀ , λ (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) (x₀ : ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) → vb₀ (the (Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) (ρ₀ , x₀))))
  npair : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (c1₀ : Code) (v1₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀)
    (c2₀ : Code) (v2₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) v1₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀)) ρ₀) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c1₀ , v1₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) v1₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , c2₀ , v2₀)) →
    NN (k-nf , (Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , cpair c1₀ c2₀ , λ ρ₀ → (v1₀ ρ₀ , v2₀ ρ₀)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- typing derivations, typed codes
-- Der (Γ , A , c , v): c is a code of type A in Γ with meaning v. The object theory's conversion is
-- the language's judgmental equality of meanings, so there is no conversion rule: a β-redex's
-- meaning is already its contractum's.
-- constructor binders subscripted ₀: t46
data Der : (J : Jdg) → Type 1 where
  dvar : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (A₀ : PTy (Env Γ₀)) (n₀ : Word) (v₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) A₀ ρ₀) →
    Var Γ₀ A₀ n₀ v₀ → Der ((Γ₀ , A₀ , cvar n₀ , v₀))
  dapp : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (f₀ : Code) (vf₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀)
    (c₀ : Code) (va₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) , f₀ , vf₀)) → Der ((Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c₀ , va₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) va₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , capp f₀ c₀ , λ ρ₀ → vf₀ ρ₀ (va₀ ρ₀)))
  dfst : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (p₀ : Code) (vp₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , p₀ , vp₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , cfst p₀ , λ ρ₀ → fst (vp₀ ρ₀)))
  dsnd : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (p₀ : Code) (vp₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) ρ₀) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , p₀ , vp₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) (λ ρ₀ → fst (vp₀ ρ₀)) (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , csnd p₀ , λ ρ₀ → snd (vp₀ ρ₀)))
  dcase : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) (P₀ : PTy (Env (ext Γ₀ (s-bool , B₀)))) (x₀ : Code) (vx₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → Bool)
    (t₀ : Code) (vt₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → true) P₀) ρ₀)
    (f₀ : Code) (vf₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → false) P₀) ρ₀) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , x₀ , vx₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → true) P₀ , t₀ , vt₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) (λ ρ₀ → false) P₀ , f₀ , vf₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (s-bool , B₀) vx₀ P₀ , c-case t₀ f₀ x₀ ,
          λ ρ₀ → bool-elim (λ b₀ → ElP (Env (ext Γ₀ (s-bool , B₀))) P₀ (ρ₀ , b₀)) (vt₀ ρ₀) (vf₀ ρ₀) (vx₀ ρ₀)))
  dtrue : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) → Der ((Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , c-true , λ ρ₀ → true))
  dfalse : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (B₀ : Env Γ₀ → One1) → Der ((Γ₀ , (s-bool , B₀) , c-false , λ ρ₀ → false))
  dlam : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (c₀ : Code) (vb₀ : (ρ₀ : Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) → ElP (Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) →
    Der ((ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c₀ , vb₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-pi a₀ b₀ , T₀) , clam c₀ , λ (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) (x₀ : ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀) → vb₀ (the (Env (ext Γ₀ (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀))) (ρ₀ , x₀))))
  dpair : (Γ₀ : Ctx) (a₀ b₀ : TyShape) (T₀ : Env Γ₀ → Fam a₀ b₀)
    (c1₀ : Code) (v1₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) ρ₀)
    (c2₀ : Code) (v2₀ : (ρ₀ : Env Γ₀) → ElP (Env Γ₀) (at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) v1₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀)) ρ₀) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀ , c1₀ , v1₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , at-last (Env Γ₀) (dom (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) v1₀ (cod (Env Γ₀) a₀ b₀ T₀) , c2₀ , v2₀)) →
    Der ((Γ₀ , (s-sig a₀ b₀ , T₀) , cpair c1₀ c2₀ , λ ρ₀ → (v1₀ ρ₀ , v2₀ ρ₀)))
-- typed codes (paper §6.1): Code(Γ, A) = Σ c. Der(Γ, c, A), the meaning carried with the derivation
TCode : (Γ : Ctx) → PTy (Env Γ) → Type 1
TCode Γ A = (c : Code) × (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) × Der (Γ , A , c , v)
-- evaluation (6.1): eval_{Γ,A} : Code(Γ, A) → Π ρ : Env(Γ). ⟦A⟧ρ
teval : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → TCode Γ A → (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ
teval Γ A t = fst (snd t)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- worlds: renamings
-- Ren Δ Γ r: every variable of Γ is a variable of Δ, at the type pulled back along r and with the
-- meaning precomposed with r (r is the renaming's meaning, a map of environments). Worlds are these
-- functions, so identity and composition are definitional.
Ren : (Δ Γ : Ctx) → (Env Δ → Env Γ) → Type 1
Ren Δ Γ r = (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (n : Word) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) →
  Var Γ A n v → (m : Word) × Var Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A) m (λ ρ → v (r ρ))
ren-id : (Γ : Ctx) → Ren Γ Γ (λ ρ → ρ)
ren-id Γ A n v x = (n , x)
ren-comp : (Δ2 Δ1 Γ : Ctx) (r1 : Env Δ1 → Env Γ) (r2 : Env Δ2 → Env Δ1) →
  Ren Δ1 Γ r1 → Ren Δ2 Δ1 r2 → Ren Δ2 Γ (λ ρ → r1 (r2 ρ))
ren-comp Δ2 Δ1 Γ r1 r2 w1 w2 A n v x =
  let y = w1 A n v x in w2 (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ1) r1 A) (fst y) (λ ρ → v (r1 ρ)) (snd y)
-- the world one entry larger (refl at an explicit level: t50)
ren-wk : (Γ : Ctx) (B : PTy (Env Γ)) → Ren (ext Γ B) Γ (λ ρ → fst ρ)
ren-wk Γ B A n v x = (%wsucc n , inr1 ((A , n , v) , x , refl {lsuc lzero}))
-- the world one dimension larger (P2.2): every variable one index further
ren-dim : (Γ : Ctx) → Ren (lcons e-dim (fst Γ) , snd Γ) Γ (λ ρ → ρ)
ren-dim Γ A n v x = (%wsucc n , ((A , n , v) , x , λ i → (A , %wsucc n , v)))
-- a renaming under a binder
ren-keep : (Δ Γ : Ctx) (r : Env Δ → Env Γ) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → Ren Δ Γ r →
  Ren (ext Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A)) (ext Γ A) (λ p → (r (fst p) , snd p))
ren-keep Δ Γ r A w X n v (inl1 p) =
  (#0 , inl1 (λ i → (pull (Env (ext Γ A)) (Env (ext Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A))) (λ q → (r (fst q) , snd q)) (fst (p i)) ,
                     #0 , λ q → snd (snd (p i)) (r (fst q) , snd q))))
ren-keep Δ Γ r A w X n v (inr1 y) =
  let z = w (fst (fst y)) (fst (snd (fst y))) (snd (snd (fst y))) (fst (snd y))
  in (%wsucc (fst z) ,
      inr1 ((pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r (fst (fst y)) , fst z , λ ρ → snd (snd (fst y)) (r ρ)) , snd z ,
            λ i → (pull (Env (ext Γ A)) (Env (ext Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A))) (λ q → (r (fst q) , snd q)) (fst (snd (snd y) i)) ,
                   %wsucc (fst z) , λ q → snd (snd (snd (snd y) i)) (r (fst q) , snd q))))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- renaming normal forms
-- a judgment pulled back along a renaming (its code left to be computed)
NNat : NK → (Δ Γ : Ctx) (r : Env Δ → Env Γ) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (v : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) → Type 1
NNat k Δ Γ r A v = (c : Code) × NN (k , (Δ , pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A , c , λ ρ → v (r ρ)))
ren-nn : {KJ : NK × Jdg} → NN KJ → (Δ : Ctx) (r : Env Δ → Env (fst (snd KJ))) → Ren Δ (fst (snd KJ)) r →
  NNat (fst KJ) Δ (fst (snd KJ)) r (fst (snd (snd KJ))) (snd (snd (snd (snd KJ))))
ren-nn (nvar Γ A n v x) Δ r w =
  let y = w A n v x in (cvar (fst y) , nvar Δ (pull (Env Γ) (Env Δ) r A) (fst y) (λ ρ → v (r ρ)) (snd y))
ren-nn (napp Γ a b T f vf c va nf na) Δ r w =
  let rf = ren-nn nf Δ r w
      ra = ren-nn na Δ r w
  in (capp (fst rf) (fst ra) , napp Δ a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst rf) (λ ρ → vf (r ρ)) (fst ra) (λ ρ → va (r ρ)) (snd rf) (snd ra))
ren-nn (nfst Γ a b T p vp np) Δ r w =
  let rp = ren-nn np Δ r w in (cfst (fst rp) , nfst Δ a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst rp) (λ ρ → vp (r ρ)) (snd rp))
ren-nn (nsnd Γ a b T p vp np) Δ r w =
  let rp = ren-nn np Δ r w in (csnd (fst rp) , nsnd Δ a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst rp) (λ ρ → vp (r ρ)) (snd rp))
ren-nn (ncase Γ B P x vx t vt f vf nx nt nf) Δ r w =
  let rx = ren-nn nx Δ r w
      rt = ren-nn nt Δ r w
      rf = ren-nn nf Δ r w
  in (c-case (fst rt) (fst rf) (fst rx) ,
      ncase Δ (λ ρ → B (r ρ)) (pull (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) (Env (ext Δ (s-bool , λ ρ → B (r ρ)))) (λ p → (r (fst p) , snd p)) P)
        (fst rx) (λ ρ → vx (r ρ)) (fst rt) (λ ρ → vt (r ρ)) (fst rf) (λ ρ → vf (r ρ)) (snd rx) (snd rt) (snd rf))
ren-nn (nne Γ B x vx nx) Δ r w =
  let rx = ren-nn nx Δ r w in (fst rx , nne Δ (λ ρ → B (r ρ)) (fst rx) (λ ρ → vx (r ρ)) (snd rx))
ren-nn (ntrue Γ B) Δ r w = (c-true , ntrue Δ (λ ρ → B (r ρ)))
ren-nn (nfalse Γ B) Δ r w = (c-false , nfalse Δ (λ ρ → B (r ρ)))
ren-nn (nlam Γ a b T c vb nb) Δ r w =
  let rb = ren-nn nb (ext Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)))) (λ p → (r (fst p) , snd p)) (ren-keep Δ Γ r (dom (Env Γ) a b T) w)
  in (clam (fst rb) , nlam Δ a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst rb) (λ p → vb (r (fst p) , snd p)) (snd rb))
ren-nn (npair Γ a b T c1 v1 c2 v2 n1 n2) Δ r w =
  let r1 = ren-nn n1 Δ r w
      r2 = ren-nn n2 Δ r w
  in (cpair (fst r1) (fst r2) , npair Δ a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst r1) (λ ρ → v1 (r ρ)) (fst r2) (λ ρ → v2 (r ρ)) (snd r1) (snd r2))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- computability (the Kripke logical relation)
-- CompS s Δ T x: x, at world Δ, is computable at the type of shape s given by T. By recursion on the
-- shape, so it computes at open worlds and environments. Bool: x is true, or false, or a neutral (a
-- closed sum with explicit equations, so that case analysis needs no matching of an indexed family
-- at a computed index, t47). Π: at every later world, a computable argument gives a computable
-- result. Σ: both components.
-- (PathP for Path: t50)
CompS : (s : TyShape) (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) → Type 1
CompS s-bool Δ T x =
  Sum1 (PathP (λ i → (ρ : Env Δ) → Bool) x (λ ρ → true) × One1)
       (Sum1 (PathP (λ i → (ρ : Env Δ) → Bool) x (λ ρ → false) × One1)
             ((c : Code) × NN (k-ne , (Δ , (s-bool , T) , c , x))))
CompS (s-pi a b) Δ T x =
  (Δ' : Ctx) (r : Env Δ' → Env Δ) → Ren Δ' Δ r →
  (y : (ρ : Env Δ') → El a (fst (T (r ρ)))) → CompS a Δ' (λ ρ → fst (T (r ρ))) y →
  CompS b Δ' (λ ρ → snd (T (r ρ)) (y ρ)) (λ ρ → x (r ρ) (y ρ))
CompS (s-sig a b) Δ T x =
  CompS a Δ (λ ρ → fst (T ρ)) (λ ρ → fst (x ρ)) × CompS b Δ (λ ρ → snd (T ρ) (fst (x ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (x ρ))
-- at a type over a context's environments
Comp : (G : Type 1) (A : PTy G) (Δ : Ctx) (δ : Env Δ → G) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → ElP G A (δ ρ)) → Type 1
Comp G A Δ δ x = CompS (fst A) Δ (λ ρ → snd A (δ ρ)) x
-- monotonicity: computability is kept along a renaming
comp-ren : (s : TyShape) (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) →
  CompS s Δ T x → (Δ' : Ctx) (r : Env Δ' → Env Δ) → Ren Δ' Δ r → CompS s Δ' (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (λ ρ → x (r ρ))
comp-ren s-bool Δ T x (inl1 p) Δ' r w = inl1 ((λ i ρ → fst p i (r ρ)) , one)
comp-ren s-bool Δ T x (inr1 (inl1 p)) Δ' r w = inr1 (inl1 ((λ i ρ → fst p i (r ρ)) , one))
comp-ren s-bool Δ T x (inr1 (inr1 n)) Δ' r w = inr1 (inr1 (ren-nn (snd n) Δ' r w))
comp-ren (s-pi a b) Δ T x cx Δ' r w =
  λ Δ2 r2 w2 y cy → cx Δ2 (λ ρ → r (r2 ρ)) (ren-comp Δ2 Δ' Δ r r2 w w2) y cy
comp-ren (s-sig a b) Δ T x cx Δ' r w =
  (comp-ren a Δ (λ ρ → fst (T ρ)) (λ ρ → fst (x ρ)) (fst cx) Δ' r w ,
   comp-ren b Δ (λ ρ → snd (T ρ) (fst (x ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (x ρ)) (snd cx) Δ' r w)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- reify and reflect (paper §6.1)
-- reify reads a computable value back as a normal form whose meaning is exactly the value; reflect
-- makes a neutral computable. Both by recursion on the shape, as one function (mutual definitions
-- by clauses are not available); each shape's clauses take the components' pair as arguments. The
-- Π clauses are the paper's Kripke clauses: reify applies the value, at the world one variable
-- larger, to that variable reflected; reflect applies the neutral to the reified argument, at the
-- later world.
Reify : TyShape → Type 1
Reify s = (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) →
  CompS s Δ T x → (c : Code) × NN (k-nf , (Δ , (s , T) , c , x))
Reflect : TyShape → Type 1
Reflect s = (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) (c : Code) →
  NN (k-ne , (Δ , (s , T) , c , x)) → CompS s Δ T x
-- (refl at an explicit level: t50)
vz : (Δ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Δ)) → Var (ext Δ A) (wk Δ A A) #0 (λ ρ → snd ρ)
vz Δ A = inl1 (refl {lsuc lzero})
var0 : (Δ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Δ)) → NN (k-ne , (ext Δ A , wk Δ A A , cvar #0 , λ ρ → snd ρ))
var0 Δ A = nvar (ext Δ A) (wk Δ A A) #0 (λ ρ → snd ρ) (vz Δ A)
-- (the world one larger, its variable reflected, written out: let-bound values are not unfolded in
-- the types of what follows, so this is a separate definition)
reify-pi-body : (a b : TyShape) → Reify a × Reflect a → Reify b × Reflect b →
  (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Fam a b) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El (s-pi a b) (T ρ)) → CompS (s-pi a b) Δ T x →
  (c : Code) × NN (k-nf , (ext Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T) , cod (Env Δ) a b T , c , λ ρ → x (fst ρ) (snd ρ)))
reify-pi-body a b ra rb Δ T x f =
  fst rb (ext Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T)) (λ ρ → snd (T (fst ρ)) (snd ρ)) (λ ρ → x (fst ρ) (snd ρ))
    (f (ext Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T)) (λ ρ → fst ρ) (ren-wk Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T)) (λ ρ → snd ρ)
       (snd ra (ext Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T)) (λ ρ → fst (T (fst ρ))) (λ ρ → snd ρ) (cvar #0) (var0 Δ (dom (Env Δ) a b T))))
-- at Bool: true and false by their equations, a neutral as itself
reify-bool : Reify s-bool
reify-bool Δ T x (inl1 p) =
  (c-true , transport (λ i → NN (k-nf , (Δ , (s-bool , T) , c-true , fst p (~ i)))) (ntrue Δ T))
reify-bool Δ T x (inr1 (inl1 p)) =
  (c-false , transport (λ i → NN (k-nf , (Δ , (s-bool , T) , c-false , fst p (~ i)))) (nfalse Δ T))
reify-bool Δ T x (inr1 (inr1 n)) = (fst n , nne Δ T (fst n) x (snd n))
reify-pi : (a b : TyShape) → Reify a × Reflect a → Reify b × Reflect b → Reify (s-pi a b)
reify-pi a b ra rb Δ T x f =
  (clam (fst (reify-pi-body a b ra rb Δ T x f)) ,
   nlam Δ a b T (fst (reify-pi-body a b ra rb Δ T x f)) (λ ρ → x (fst ρ) (snd ρ)) (snd (reify-pi-body a b ra rb Δ T x f)))
reflect-pi : (a b : TyShape) → Reify a × Reflect a → Reify b × Reflect b → Reflect (s-pi a b)
reflect-pi a b ra rb Δ T x c n Δ' r w y cy =
  let rn = ren-nn n Δ' r w
      rarg = fst ra Δ' (λ ρ → fst (T (r ρ))) y cy
  in snd rb Δ' (λ ρ → snd (T (r ρ)) (y ρ)) (λ ρ → x (r ρ) (y ρ)) (capp (fst rn) (fst rarg))
       (napp Δ' a b (λ ρ → T (r ρ)) (fst rn) (λ ρ → x (r ρ)) (fst rarg) y (snd rn) (snd rarg))
reify-sig : (a b : TyShape) → Reify a × Reflect a → Reify b × Reflect b → Reify (s-sig a b)
reify-sig a b ra rb Δ T x cx =
  let c1 = fst ra Δ (λ ρ → fst (T ρ)) (λ ρ → fst (x ρ)) (fst cx)
      c2 = fst rb Δ (λ ρ → snd (T ρ) (fst (x ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (x ρ)) (snd cx)
  in (cpair (fst c1) (fst c2) , npair Δ a b T (fst c1) (λ ρ → fst (x ρ)) (fst c2) (λ ρ → snd (x ρ)) (snd c1) (snd c2))
reflect-sig : (a b : TyShape) → Reify a × Reflect a → Reify b × Reflect b → Reflect (s-sig a b)
reflect-sig a b ra rb Δ T x c n =
  (snd ra Δ (λ ρ → fst (T ρ)) (λ ρ → fst (x ρ)) (cfst c) (nfst Δ a b T c x n) ,
   snd rb Δ (λ ρ → snd (T ρ) (fst (x ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (x ρ)) (csnd c) (nsnd Δ a b T c x n))
rr : (s : TyShape) → Reify s × Reflect s
rr s-bool = (reify-bool , λ Δ T x c n → inr1 (inr1 (c , n)))
rr (s-pi a b) = (reify-pi a b (rr a) (rr b) , reflect-pi a b (rr a) (rr b))
rr (s-sig a b) = (reify-sig a b (rr a) (rr b) , reflect-sig a b (rr a) (rr b))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- computable environments
-- CompEnv sk γ Δ δ: every entry of the environment δ (seen at world Δ) is computable at its type;
-- by recursion on the skeleton
CompEnv : (sk : Lst Entry) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) (Δ : Ctx) → (Env Δ → Env (sk , γ)) → Type 1
CompEnv lnil γ Δ δ = One1
CompEnv (lcons e-dim sk) γ Δ δ = CompEnv sk γ Δ δ
CompEnv (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ Δ δ =
  CompEnv sk (fst γ) Δ (λ ρ → fst (δ ρ)) × CompS s Δ (λ ρ → snd γ (fst (δ ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (δ ρ))
env-ren : (sk : Lst Entry) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) (Δ : Ctx) (δ : Env Δ → Env (sk , γ)) → CompEnv sk γ Δ δ →
  (Δ' : Ctx) (r : Env Δ' → Env Δ) → Ren Δ' Δ r → CompEnv sk γ Δ' (λ ρ → δ (r ρ))
env-ren lnil γ Δ δ e Δ' r w = e
env-ren (lcons e-dim sk) γ Δ δ e Δ' r w = env-ren sk γ Δ δ e Δ' r w
env-ren (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ Δ δ e Δ' r w =
  (env-ren sk (fst γ) Δ (λ ρ → fst (δ ρ)) (fst e) Δ' r w ,
   comp-ren s Δ (λ ρ → snd γ (fst (δ ρ))) (λ ρ → snd (δ ρ)) (snd e) Δ' r w)
-- a variable's value in a computable environment is computable
var-comp : (sk : Lst Entry) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) (X : VIx (Env (sk , γ))) → VarT sk γ X →
  (Δ : Ctx) (δ : Env Δ → Env (sk , γ)) → CompEnv sk γ Δ δ →
  Comp (Env (sk , γ)) (fst X) Δ δ (λ ρ → snd (snd X) (δ ρ))
var-comp lnil γ X x Δ δ e = Empty-rec (fst x)
var-comp (lcons e-dim sk) γ X y Δ δ e =
  transport (λ i → Comp (Env (sk , γ)) (fst (snd (snd y) (~ i))) Δ δ (λ ρ → snd (snd (snd (snd y) (~ i))) (δ ρ)))
    (var-comp sk γ (fst y) (fst (snd y)) Δ δ e)
var-comp (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ X (inl1 p) Δ δ e =
  transport (λ i → Comp (Env (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ)) (fst (p (~ i))) Δ δ (λ ρ → snd (snd (p (~ i))) (δ ρ))) (snd e)
var-comp (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ X (inr1 y) Δ δ e =
  transport (λ i → Comp (Env (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ)) (fst (snd (snd y) (~ i))) Δ δ (λ ρ → snd (snd (snd (snd y) (~ i))) (δ ρ)))
    (var-comp sk (fst γ) (fst y) (fst (snd y)) Δ (λ ρ → fst (δ ρ)) (fst e))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the fundamental lemma
-- case on a computable Bool: true and false by their equations, a neutral by the neutral case with
-- its branches reified (the meaning is the language's own dependent case, so where the scrutinee is
-- a constant the branch's computability is the result's definitionally)
case-comp : (Γ : Ctx) (B : Env Γ → One1) (P : PTy (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B)))) (vx : (ρ : Env Γ) → Bool)
  (vt : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (s-bool , B) (λ ρ → true) P) ρ)
  (vf : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (s-bool , B) (λ ρ → false) P) ρ)
  (Δ : Ctx) (δ : Env Δ → Env Γ) →
  CompS s-bool Δ (λ ρ → B (δ ρ)) (λ ρ → vx (δ ρ)) →
  Comp (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (s-bool , B) (λ ρ → true) P) Δ δ (λ ρ → vt (δ ρ)) →
  Comp (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (s-bool , B) (λ ρ → false) P) Δ δ (λ ρ → vf (δ ρ)) →
  Comp (Env Γ) (at-last (Env Γ) (s-bool , B) vx P) Δ δ
    (λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) P (δ ρ , b)) (vt (δ ρ)) (vf (δ ρ)) (vx (δ ρ)))
case-comp Γ B P vx vt vf Δ δ (inl1 p) ct cf =
  transport (λ i → CompS (fst P) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , fst p (~ i) ρ))
                     (λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) P (δ ρ , b)) (vt (δ ρ)) (vf (δ ρ)) (fst p (~ i) ρ)))
    ct
case-comp Γ B P vx vt vf Δ δ (inr1 (inl1 p)) ct cf =
  transport (λ i → CompS (fst P) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , fst p (~ i) ρ))
                     (λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) P (δ ρ , b)) (vt (δ ρ)) (vf (δ ρ)) (fst p (~ i) ρ)))
    cf
case-comp Γ B P vx vt vf Δ δ (inr1 (inr1 n)) ct cf =
  snd (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , vx (δ ρ)))
    (λ ρ → bool-elim (λ b → ElP (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) P (δ ρ , b)) (vt (δ ρ)) (vf (δ ρ)) (vx (δ ρ)))
    (c-case (fst (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , true)) (λ ρ → vt (δ ρ)) ct))
            (fst (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , false)) (λ ρ → vf (δ ρ)) cf))
            (fst n))
    (ncase Δ (λ ρ → B (δ ρ))
       (pull (Env (ext Γ (s-bool , B))) (Env (ext Δ (s-bool , λ ρ → B (δ ρ)))) (λ q → (δ (fst q) , snd q)) P)
       (fst n) (λ ρ → vx (δ ρ))
       (fst (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , true)) (λ ρ → vt (δ ρ)) ct)) (λ ρ → vt (δ ρ))
       (fst (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , false)) (λ ρ → vf (δ ρ)) cf)) (λ ρ → vf (δ ρ))
       (snd n)
       (snd (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , true)) (λ ρ → vt (δ ρ)) ct))
       (snd (fst (rr (fst P)) Δ (λ ρ → snd P (δ ρ , false)) (λ ρ → vf (δ ρ)) cf)))
-- the fundamental lemma: a derivation's meaning is computable at every world under every computable
-- environment (by recursion on the derivation; its binder case is the paper's weakening/application
-- calculation; its Bool constants' equations are path λs, not refl: t50)
fund : {J : Jdg} → Der J → (Δ : Ctx) (δ : Env Δ → Env (fst J)) → CompEnv (fst (fst J)) (snd (fst J)) Δ δ →
  Comp (Env (fst J)) (fst (snd J)) Δ δ (λ ρ → snd (snd (snd J)) (δ ρ))
fund (dvar Γ A n v x) Δ δ e = var-comp (fst Γ) (snd Γ) (A , n , v) x Δ δ e
fund (dapp Γ a b T f vf c va df da) Δ δ e = fund df Δ δ e Δ (λ ρ → ρ) (ren-id Δ) (λ ρ → va (δ ρ)) (fund da Δ δ e)
fund (dfst Γ a b T p vp dp) Δ δ e = fst (fund dp Δ δ e)
fund (dsnd Γ a b T p vp dp) Δ δ e = snd (fund dp Δ δ e)
fund (dcase Γ B P x vx t vt f vf dx dt df) Δ δ e =
  case-comp Γ B P vx vt vf Δ δ (fund dx Δ δ e) (fund dt Δ δ e) (fund df Δ δ e)
fund (dtrue Γ B) Δ δ e = inl1 ((λ i ρ → true) , one)
fund (dfalse Γ B) Δ δ e = inr1 (inl1 ((λ i ρ → false) , one))
fund (dlam Γ a b T c vb db) Δ δ e =
  λ Δ' r w y cy → fund db Δ' (λ ρ → (δ (r ρ) , y ρ)) (env-ren (fst Γ) (snd Γ) Δ δ e Δ' r w , cy)
fund (dpair Γ a b T c1 v1 c2 v2 d1 d2) Δ δ e = (fund d1 Δ δ e , fund d2 Δ δ e)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- normalization, reifySound (6.5)
-- the identity environment with every variable reflected (paper: reflectContext)
reflect-env : (sk : Lst Entry) (γ : fst (CtxE sk)) → CompEnv sk γ (sk , γ) (λ ρ → ρ)
reflect-env lnil γ = one
reflect-env (lcons e-dim sk) γ = env-ren sk γ (sk , γ) (λ ρ → ρ) (reflect-env sk γ) (lcons e-dim sk , γ) (λ ρ → ρ) (ren-dim (sk , γ))
reflect-env (lcons (e-ty s) sk) γ =
  (env-ren sk (fst γ) (sk , fst γ) (λ ρ → ρ) (reflect-env sk (fst γ)) (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ) (λ ρ → fst ρ) (ren-wk (sk , fst γ) (s , snd γ)) ,
   snd (rr s) (lcons (e-ty s) sk , γ) (λ ρ → snd γ (fst ρ)) (λ ρ → snd ρ) (cvar #0) (var0 (sk , fst γ) (s , snd γ)))
-- normal and neutral forms are derivations, with the same code and meaning
embed : {KJ : NK × Jdg} → NN KJ → Der (snd KJ)
embed (nvar Γ A n v x) = dvar Γ A n v x
embed (napp Γ a b T f vf c va nf na) = dapp Γ a b T f vf c va (embed nf) (embed na)
embed (nfst Γ a b T p vp np) = dfst Γ a b T p vp (embed np)
embed (nsnd Γ a b T p vp np) = dsnd Γ a b T p vp (embed np)
embed (ncase Γ B P x vx t vt f vf nx nt nf) = dcase Γ B P x vx t vt f vf (embed nx) (embed nt) (embed nf)
embed (nne Γ B x vx nx) = embed nx
embed (ntrue Γ B) = dtrue Γ B
embed (nfalse Γ B) = dfalse Γ B
embed (nlam Γ a b T c vb nb) = dlam Γ a b T c vb (embed nb)
embed (npair Γ a b T c1 v1 c2 v2 n1 n2) = dpair Γ a b T c1 v1 c2 v2 (embed n1) (embed n2)
-- normalize Γ,A (t) = reify (eval_nf (t, reflectContext Γ)): a normal form with t's meaning
normalize-nf : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (t : TCode Γ A) → (c : Code) × NN (k-nf , (Γ , A , c , teval Γ A t))
normalize-nf Γ A t =
  fst (rr (fst A)) Γ (snd A) (teval Γ A t) (fund (snd (snd t)) Γ (λ ρ → ρ) (reflect-env (fst Γ) (snd Γ)))
-- as a typed code (paper: normalize : Code(Γ, A) → Code(Γ, A))
normalize : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) → TCode Γ A → TCode Γ A
normalize Γ A t = (fst (normalize-nf Γ A t) , teval Γ A t , embed (snd (normalize-nf Γ A t)))
-- reify as a map into typed codes, and its fundamental equation (6.5): for every computable value v
-- at every world, eval (reify v) ρ ≡ v ρ, at every environment ρ; it holds by the indices
-- a normal form packaged as a typed code (a separate definition because of t48)
nf-code : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (x : (ρ : Env Γ) → ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) → ((c : Code) × NN (k-nf , (Γ , A , c , x))) → TCode Γ A
nf-code Γ A x p = (fst p , x , embed (snd p))
reify-code : (s : TyShape) (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) → CompS s Δ T x → TCode Δ (s , T)
reify-code s Δ T x cx = nf-code Δ (s , T) x (fst (rr s) Δ T x cx)
reifySound : (s : TyShape) (Δ : Ctx) (T : Env Δ → Sem s) (x : (ρ : Env Δ) → El s (T ρ)) (cx : CompS s Δ T x) (ρ : Env Δ) →
  Path (El s (T ρ)) (teval Δ (s , T) (reify-code s Δ T x cx) ρ) (x ρ)
reifySound s Δ T x cx ρ = refl
-- normalization preserves meaning
normalize-sound : (Γ : Ctx) (A : PTy (Env Γ)) (t : TCode Γ A) (ρ : Env Γ) →
  Path (ElP (Env Γ) A ρ) (teval Γ A (normalize Γ A t) ρ) (teval Γ A t ρ)
normalize-sound Γ A t ρ = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: lines and cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A line in X: two points and a path between them; its endpoints are the path's own
-- judgmentally (p 0 ≡ x0). An n-cube: an (n-1)-cube of lines, so the newest dimension is the
-- innermost and an n-cube of lines is literally an (n+1)-cube (a path λ's body, a PathP's meaning).
-- The interval enters only through PathP; operations are functions applied to `p i` under a path λ.
Line : Type 1 → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
Line X = (lx0 : X) × (lx1 : X) × PathP (λ i → X) lx0 lx1
Cube : Nat → Type 1 → Type 1
Cube zero X = X
Cube (suc n) X = Cube n (Line X)
line-map : (X Y : Type 1) → (X → Y) → Line X → Line Y
line-map X Y f L = (f (fst L) , f (fst (snd L)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i))
cube-map : (n : Nat) (X Y : Type 1) → (X → Y) → Cube n X → Cube n Y
cube-map zero X Y f c = f c
cube-map (suc n) X Y f c = cube-map n (Line X) (Line Y) (line-map X Y f) c
-- the generators of the cube category at the newest dimension, on lines (an n-cube's are their
-- cube-maps): the two faces, the degeneracy, reversal, the connections ∧ and ∨, exchange of the two
-- newest dimensions and their diagonal
face0-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → X
face0-l X L = fst L
face1-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → X
face1-l X L = fst (snd L)
degen-l : (X : Type 1) → X → Line X
degen-l X x = (x , x , λ i → x)
rev-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line X
rev-l X L = (fst (snd L) , fst L , λ i → snd (snd L) (~ i))
-- λ i j → p (i ∧ j) and λ i j → p (i ∨ j) (j the newer)
meet-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line (Line X)
meet-l X L = ((fst L , fst L , λ j → fst L) , L , λ i → (fst L , snd (snd L) i , λ j → snd (snd L) (i ∧ j)))
join-l : (X : Type 1) → Line X → Line (Line X)
join-l X L = (L , (fst (snd L) , fst (snd L) , λ j → fst (snd L)) , λ i → (snd (snd L) i , fst (snd L) , λ j → snd (snd L) (i ∨ j)))
-- λ i j → q j i
exch-l : (X : Type 1) → Line (Line X) → Line (Line X)
exch-l X Q =
  ((fst (fst Q) , fst (fst (snd Q)) , λ i → fst (snd (snd Q) i)) ,
   (fst (snd (fst Q)) , fst (snd (fst (snd Q))) , λ i → fst (snd (snd (snd Q) i))) ,
   λ j → (snd (snd (fst Q)) j , snd (snd (fst (snd Q))) j , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd Q) i)) j))
-- λ i → q i i
diag-l : (X : Type 1) → Line (Line X) → Line X
diag-l X Q = (fst (fst Q) , fst (snd (fst (snd Q))) , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd Q) i)) i)
-- their laws hold by refl (the endpoints of a path are its own judgmentally); the type is a line,
-- so the laws are PathPs (t50)
face0-degen : (X : Type 1) (x : X) → PathP (λ i → X) (face0-l X (degen-l X x)) x
face0-degen X x = λ i → x
rev-rev : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (rev-l X (rev-l X L)) L
rev-rev X L = λ i → L
exch-exch : (X : Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → PathP (λ i → Line (Line X)) (exch-l X (exch-l X Q)) Q
exch-exch X Q = λ i → Q
diag-degen : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (diag-l X (degen-l (Line X) L)) L
diag-degen X L = λ i → L
diag-meet : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (diag-l X (meet-l X L)) L
diag-meet X L = λ i → L
face1-meet : (X : Type 1) (L : Line X) → PathP (λ i → Line X) (face1-l (Line X) (meet-l X L)) L
face1-meet X L = λ i → L
-- composition of cube maps: at a variable dimension it does not hold by refl (refused, "wrong
-- endpoint at 0", 2026-11-12: cube-map is stuck on n); it holds as a path, by induction
cube-comp : (n : Nat) (X Y Z : Type 1) (f : Y → Z) (g : X → Y) (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c)
cube-comp zero X Y Z f g c = λ i → f (g c)
cube-comp (suc n) X Y Z f g c = cube-comp n (Line X) (Line Y) (Line Z) (line-map Y Z f) (line-map X Y g) c
cube-id : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (c : Cube n X) → PathP (λ i → Cube n X) (cube-map n X X (λ x → x) c) c
cube-id zero X c = λ i → c
cube-id (suc n) X c = cube-id n (Line X) c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: interval expressions, De Morgan normal forms
-- (2026-11-12) The interval of CCHM is the free De Morgan algebra on the dimension variables, which is
-- the free distributive lattice (with 0, 1) on the literals i and ~i; an element's canonical form is
-- an antichain of conjunctions of literals (a DNF with absorption), each conjunction a set of
-- literals. Interval expressions are the codes ci0, ci1, cvar k, cneg, cmeet, cjoin (the one code
-- representation); dnf-of reads one to its canonical form and dnf-code writes the form back. A
-- neutral path application is formed at a canonical, non-constant form only (P2.6), so that no normal
-- form applies a neutral path at an endpoint or at two spellings of one interval element.
-- a literal: a dimension variable and its polarity (true: i, false: ~i); ordered by variable, then ~i
-- before i
Lit : Type
Lit = Word × Bool
bool-eq : Bool → Bool → Bool
bool-eq true b = b
bool-eq false b = not b
lit-eq : Lit → Lit → Bool
lit-eq a b = andB (weq (fst a) (fst b)) (bool-eq (snd a) (snd b))
lit-lt : Lit → Lit → Bool
lit-lt a b = if wlt (fst a) (fst b) then true else (if weq (fst a) (fst b) then andB (not (snd a)) (snd b) else false)
-- a conjunction: a strictly increasing list of literals; a form: a list of conjunctions
Conj : Type
Conj = Lst Lit
DNF : Type
DNF = Lst Conj
-- the conjunction of two conjunctions (their union, as an ordered merge); by recursion on the first,
-- the second inserted literal by literal
conj-ins : Lit → Conj → Conj
conj-ins l lnil = lcons l lnil
conj-ins l (lcons m ms) = if lit-eq l m then lcons m ms else (if lit-lt l m then lcons l (lcons m ms) else lcons m (conj-ins l ms))
conj-meet : Conj → Conj → Conj
conj-meet lnil d = d
conj-meet (lcons l ls) d = conj-ins l (conj-meet ls d)
-- membership and inclusion
conj-has : Lit → Conj → Bool
conj-has l lnil = false
conj-has l (lcons m ms) = if lit-eq l m then true else conj-has l ms
conj-sub : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-sub lnil d = true
conj-sub (lcons l ls) d = andB (conj-has l d) (conj-sub ls d)
-- equality of conjunctions as lists (a canonical conjunction is ordered, so this is set equality there)
conj-eq : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-eq lnil lnil = true
conj-eq lnil (lcons m ms) = false
conj-eq (lcons l ls) lnil = false
conj-eq (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = andB (lit-eq l m) (conj-eq ls ms)
-- the order of conjunctions in a canonical form: shorter first, then by their first differing literal
conj-lt : Conj → Conj → Bool
conj-lt lnil lnil = false
conj-lt lnil (lcons m ms) = true
conj-lt (lcons l ls) lnil = false
conj-lt (lcons l ls) (lcons m ms) = if lit-lt l m then true else (if lit-eq l m then conj-lt ls ms else false)
-- adding a conjunction to a canonical form: dropped if some conjunction there is included in it
-- (absorption), else the ones that include it removed and it inserted in order
dnf-any-sub : Conj → DNF → Bool
dnf-any-sub c lnil = false
dnf-any-sub c (lcons d ds) = if conj-sub d c then true else dnf-any-sub c ds
dnf-drop-sup : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-drop-sup c lnil = lnil
dnf-drop-sup c (lcons d ds) = if conj-sub c d then dnf-drop-sup c ds else lcons d (dnf-drop-sup c ds)
dnf-insert : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-insert c lnil = lcons c lnil
dnf-insert c (lcons d ds) = if conj-lt c d then lcons c (lcons d ds) else lcons d (dnf-insert c ds)
dnf-add : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-add c f = if dnf-any-sub c f then f else dnf-insert c (dnf-drop-sup c f)
-- the lattice operations and De Morgan negation on canonical forms
dnf-join : DNF → DNF → DNF
dnf-join lnil g = g
dnf-join (lcons c cs) g = dnf-add c (dnf-join cs g)
dnf-meet-c : Conj → DNF → DNF
dnf-meet-c c lnil = lnil
dnf-meet-c c (lcons d ds) = dnf-add (conj-meet c d) (dnf-meet-c c ds)
dnf-meet : DNF → DNF → DNF
dnf-meet lnil g = lnil
dnf-meet (lcons c cs) g = dnf-join (dnf-meet-c c g) (dnf-meet cs g)
dnf-zero : DNF
dnf-zero = lnil
dnf-one : DNF
dnf-one = lcons lnil lnil
-- ~(l1 ∧ … ∧ lk) = ~l1 ∨ … ∨ ~lk, and ~(c1 ∨ … ∨ cm) = ~c1 ∧ … ∧ ~cm
neg-conj : Conj → DNF
neg-conj lnil = dnf-zero
neg-conj (lcons l ls) = dnf-add (lcons (fst l , not (snd l)) lnil) (neg-conj ls)
dnf-neg : DNF → DNF
dnf-neg lnil = dnf-one
dnf-neg (lcons c cs) = dnf-meet (neg-conj c) (dnf-neg cs)
-- an interval code's canonical form (none for a code that is not an interval expression)
dnf-of : Code → Opt DNF
dnf-of ci0 = some dnf-zero
dnf-of ci1 = some dnf-one
dnf-of (cvar k) = some (lcons (lcons (k , true) lnil) lnil)
dnf-of (cneg r) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → some (dnf-neg f)
dnf-of (cmeet r s) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → (case dnf-of s of none → none; some g → some (dnf-meet f g))
dnf-of (cjoin r s) = case dnf-of r of none → none; some f → (case dnf-of s of none → none; some g → some (dnf-join f g))
dnf-of c = none
-- a canonical form written as a code
lit-code : Lit → Code
lit-code l = if snd l then cvar (fst l) else cneg (cvar (fst l))
conj-code-from : Lit → Conj → Code
conj-code-from l lnil = lit-code l
conj-code-from l (lcons m ms) = cmeet (lit-code l) (conj-code-from m ms)
conj-code : Conj → Code
conj-code lnil = ci1
conj-code (lcons l ls) = conj-code-from l ls
dnf-code-from : Conj → DNF → Code
dnf-code-from c lnil = conj-code c
dnf-code-from c (lcons d ds) = cjoin (conj-code c) (dnf-code-from d ds)
dnf-code : DNF → Code
dnf-code lnil = ci0
dnf-code (lcons c cs) = dnf-code-from c cs
-- a form is canonical when it is its own normal form, and
-- constant when it is 0 or 1
dnf-eq : DNF → DNF → Bool
dnf-eq lnil lnil = true
dnf-eq lnil (lcons d ds) = false
dnf-eq (lcons c cs) lnil = false
dnf-eq (lcons c cs) (lcons d ds) = andB (conj-eq c d) (dnf-eq cs ds)
-- the normal form of any list of conjunctions: each conjunction ordered, then all added
dnf-norm : DNF → DNF
dnf-norm lnil = lnil
dnf-norm (lcons c cs) = dnf-add (conj-meet c lnil) (dnf-norm cs)
dnf-canon : DNF → Bool
dnf-canon f = dnf-eq (dnf-norm f) f
dnf-nonconst : DNF → Bool
dnf-nonconst lnil = false
dnf-nonconst (lcons lnil cs) = false
dnf-nonconst (lcons (lcons l ls) cs) = true

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2: skeletons with dimensions, and path application on cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A context's skeleton lists its entries, newest first: a type's shape or a dimension.
-- Codes count both (de Bruijn indices over one context of term and dimension variables, lib/code.cub);
-- a dimension contributes a direction to the cube of the judgments over the context and nothing to a
-- vertex's environment.
-- (Entry and dims are defined with the contexts, above)
-- the diagonal of the newest direction of a cube over sk with the dimension that index k of sk names
-- (exchanging the newest direction outward past each nearer dimension); an index that names a term
-- entry or nothing has no dimension, and gives the face at 0 (the side condition of a neutral path
-- application excludes it, P2.6)
diag-sk : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
diag-sk lnil k X c = face0-l X c
diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X c =
  if weq k #0 then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c
diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) k X c =
  if weq k #0 then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
-- the newest direction at a literal (i or ~i), the index shifted by o (the dimensions a connection
-- has put in front of the skeleton)
papp-lit : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-lit sk X o l c =
  if snd l then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c
  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
-- at a conjunction l ∧ m ∧ …: the connection λ i j → p (i ∧ j), then j at the rest (over the skeleton
-- with i in front, indices one further), then i at l; the empty conjunction is 1
papp-conj-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-conj-from sk X o l lnil c = papp-lit sk X o l c
papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c =
  papp-lit sk X o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
papp-conj : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-conj sk X o lnil c = cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face1-l X) c
papp-conj sk X o (lcons l ls) c = papp-conj-from sk X o l ls c
-- at a disjunction: the connection λ i j → p (i ∨ j), likewise; the empty disjunction is 0
papp-dnf-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (ds : DNF) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-dnf-from sk X o c lnil p = papp-conj sk X o c p
papp-dnf-from sk X o c (lcons d ds) p =
  papp-conj sk X o c (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) p))
-- a cube over sk with one more (newest) direction, at an interval element in canonical form over sk
papp-cube : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (f : DNF) → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X → Cube (dims sk) X
papp-cube sk X lnil p = cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) p
papp-cube sk X (lcons c cs) p = papp-dnf-from sk X #0 c cs p

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.1: cubes in a family over a cube
-- (2026-11-12) A line over a line L of X in a family Y: a point over each end and a path over L; a
-- cube over a cube likewise, one direction at a time (newest innermost, as Cube).
LineO : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → Line X → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
LineO X Y L = (ly0 : Y (fst L)) × (ly1 : Y (fst (snd L))) × PathP (λ i → Y (snd (snd L) i)) ly0 ly1
DCube : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → Cube n X → Type 1
DCube zero X Y c = Y c
DCube (suc n) X Y c = DCube n (Line X) (LineO X Y) c
lineo-map : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x → Z) → (L : Line X) → LineO X Y L → Line Z
lineo-map X Y Z f L D = (f (fst L) (fst D) , f (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
-- a map out of a cube with a cube over it
dcube-map : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x → Z) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X Y c → Cube n Z
dcube-map zero X Y Z f c d = f c d
dcube-map (suc n) X Y Z f c d = dcube-map n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (Line Z) (lineo-map X Y Z f) c d
-- the cube over a cube given by a section of the family
lineo-of : (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X Y L
lineo-of X Y f L = (f (fst L) , f (fst (snd L)) , λ i → f (snd (snd L) i))
dcube-of : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → Y x) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X Y c
dcube-of zero X Y f c = f c
dcube-of (suc n) X Y f c = dcube-of n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (lineo-of X Y f) c
-- mapping out of a cube with the cube of a section is mapping out of the cube: a path by induction
dcube-map-of : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (Y : X → Type 1) (Z : Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → Z) (g : (x : X) → Y x) (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (dcube-map n X Y Z f c (dcube-of n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f x (g x)) c)
dcube-map-of zero X Y Z f g c = λ i → f c (g c)
dcube-map-of (suc n) X Y Z f g c = dcube-map-of n (Line X) (LineO X Y) (Line Z) (lineo-map X Y Z f) (lineo-of X Y g) c

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.3: the semantic path type
-- (2026-11-12) A semantic PathP type over semantic types X with meanings E: a line of semantic types
-- and a point over each end; its meaning is the language's PathP over the line, judgmentally (the
-- clause of TyE for the path shape is this pair, P2.6).
PathS : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
PathS X E = (pL : Line X) × E (fst pL) × E (fst (snd pL))
PathE : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) → PathS X E → Type
PathE X E D = PathP (λ i → E (snd (snd (fst D)) i)) (fst (snd D)) (snd (snd D))
pathE-pathp : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (A0 A1 : X) (A : PathP (λ i → X) A0 A1) (a0 : E A0) (a1 : E A1) →
  Path Type (PathE X E ((A0 , A1 , A) , a0 , a1)) (PathP (λ i → E (A i)) a0 a1)
pathE-pathp X E A0 A1 A a0 a1 = refl
-- a value of a path type is a line over its type's line, with the type's endpoints as its ends
path-line : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (D : PathS X E) → PathE X E D →
  (y0 : E (fst (fst D))) × (y1 : E (fst (snd (fst D)))) × PathP (λ i → E (snd (snd (fst D)) i)) y0 y1
path-line X E D p = (p 0 , p 1 , p)
path-line-ends : (X : Type 1) (E : X → Type) (D : PathS X E) (p : PathE X E D) →
  Path (E (fst (fst D))) (fst (path-line X E D p)) (fst (snd D))
path-line-ends X E D p = refl

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6 foundation: maps of cubes over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A judgment over a context with dimensions is a cube of contexts G and a cube over G of
-- meanings (the head's decision of this date); these are the structural maps between such cubes, each
-- by recursion on the dimension through its line version, so each computes on constructors with no
-- path. Their composites agree only up to paths (as cube-comp).
-- the dependent eliminator of Bool into Type 1
bool-elim1 : (P : Bool → Type 1) → P true → P false → (b : Bool) → P b
bool-elim1 P t f true = t
bool-elim1 P t f false = f
-- composition and inversion of paths in a type at level 1 (PathP: t50)
pcat : (A : Type 1) (x y z : A) → PathP (λ i → A) x y → PathP (λ i → A) y z → PathP (λ i → A) x z
pcat A x y z p q = λ i → comp (λ j → A) (λ j → [ i = 0 ↦ x , i = 1 ↦ q j ]) (p i)
psym : (A : Type 1) (x y : A) → PathP (λ i → A) x y → PathP (λ i → A) y x
psym A x y p = λ i → p (~ i)
-- a fibrewise map
lineo-fmap : (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F' L
lineo-fmap X F F' h L D = (h (fst L) (fst D) , h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → h (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
dcube-fmap : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x) → (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X F' c
dcube-fmap zero X F F' h c d = h c d
dcube-fmap (suc n) X F F' h c d = dcube-fmap n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) c d
-- two cubes over one base combined fibrewise
lineo-zip : (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x → F2 x) → (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F' L → LineO X F2 L
lineo-zip X F F' F2 h L D E =
  (h (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → h (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-zip : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) → ((x : X) → F x → F' x → F2 x) → (c : Cube n X) →
  DCube n X F c → DCube n X F' c → DCube n X F2 c
dcube-zip zero X F F' F2 h c d e = h c d e
dcube-zip (suc n) X F F' F2 h c d e = dcube-zip n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F2) (lineo-zip X F F' F2 h) c d e
-- reindexing along a map of the base
lineo-reidx : (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') → ((x : X) → F x → F' (f x)) →
  (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X' F' (line-map X X' f L)
lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g L D = (g (fst L) (fst D) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i))
dcube-reidx : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') → ((x : X) → F x → F' (f x)) →
  (c : Cube n X) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X' F' (cube-map n X X' f c)
dcube-reidx zero X X' F F' f g c d = g c d
dcube-reidx (suc n) X X' F F' f g c d =
  dcube-reidx n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g) c d
-- onto a base extended by a cube over it (weakening: the new base is dcube-map f c d)
lineo-push : (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) → (L : Line X) (D : LineO X Y L) → LineO X F L → LineO X' F' (lineo-map X Y X' f L D)
lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g L D E =
  (g (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-push : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) → (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) → DCube n X F c → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d)
dcube-push zero X X' Y F F' f g c d e = g c d e
dcube-push (suc n) X X' Y F F' f g c d e =
  dcube-push n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g) c d e
-- back from such an extended base (substitution: the old base's fibres from the new one's)
lineo-pull : (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) → (L : Line X) (D : LineO X Y L) → LineO X' F' (lineo-map X Y X' f L D) → LineO X F L
lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g L D E =
  (g (fst L) (fst D) (fst E) , g (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D)) (fst (snd E)) , λ i → g (snd (snd L) i) (snd (snd D) i) (snd (snd E) i))
dcube-pull : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') →
  ((x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) → (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d) → DCube n X F c
dcube-pull zero X X' Y F F' f g c d e = g c d e
dcube-pull (suc n) X X' Y F F' f g c d e =
  dcube-pull n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g) c d e
-- the cube category's generators over their images on the base (face0-l … diag-l above)
face0-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → F (face0-l X L)
face0-o X F L D = fst D
face1-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → F (face1-l X L)
face1-o X F L D = fst (snd D)
degen-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (x : X) → F x → LineO X F (degen-l X x)
degen-o X F x y = (y , y , λ i → y)
rev-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO X F (rev-l X L)
rev-o X F L D = (fst (snd D) , fst D , λ i → snd (snd D) (~ i))
meet-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (meet-l X L)
meet-o X F L D = ((fst D , fst D , λ j → fst D) , D , λ i → (fst D , snd (snd D) i , λ j → snd (snd D) (i ∧ j)))
join-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (L : Line X) → LineO X F L → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (join-l X L)
join-o X F L D = (D , (fst (snd D) , fst (snd D) , λ j → fst (snd D)) , λ i → (snd (snd D) i , fst (snd D) , λ j → snd (snd D) (i ∨ j)))
exch-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) Q → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) (exch-l X Q)
exch-o X F Q D =
  ((fst (fst D) , fst (fst (snd D)) , λ i → fst (snd (snd D) i)) ,
   (fst (snd (fst D)) , fst (snd (fst (snd D))) , λ i → fst (snd (snd (snd D) i))) ,
   λ j → (snd (snd (fst D)) j , snd (snd (fst (snd D))) j , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd D) i)) j))
diag-o : (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (Q : Line (Line X)) → LineO (Line X) (LineO X F) Q → LineO X F (diag-l X Q)
diag-o X F Q D = (fst (fst D) , fst (snd (fst (snd D))) , λ i → snd (snd (snd (snd D) i)) i)
-- path application at any interval form to a cube degenerate in its newest direction gives the cube
-- back (a path, by induction: each generator composed with the degeneracy is judgmentally the identity
-- or a degeneracy, and composites of cube maps are cube-comp). A context's cube is degenerate in the
-- direction a path λ binds, so this carries a dpapp's meaning back over its context (P2.6).
diag-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (diag-sk sk k X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
diag-deg lnil k X G = λ i → G
diag-deg (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
          (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face0-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G))
    (diag-deg sk (%wsub k #1) X G) (weq k #0)
diag-deg (lcons e-dim sk) k X G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (suc (dims sk)) X)
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
                         (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G))) G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X)) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G))
          (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (λ x → x) G) G
          (cube-comp (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G) (cube-id (dims sk) (Line X) G))
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X)
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G)))
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (degen-l (Line X)) G)) G
          (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X)
                   (cube-comp (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) G i))
          (diag-deg sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) G))
    (weq k #0)
-- a path between cube maps whose functions agree judgmentally after composition with the degeneracy
-- (the two composites of cube maps meeting at one cube map)
cube-comp2 : (n : Nat) (X Y Y' Z : Type 1) (f : Y → Z) (g : X → Y) (f' : Y' → Z) (g' : X → Y') (c : Cube n X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c))
cube-comp2 n X Y Y' Z f g f' g' c p =
  pcat (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c))
    (pcat (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y Z f (cube-map n X Y g c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f (g x)) c) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c)
       (cube-comp n X Y Z f g c) p)
    (psym (Cube n Z) (cube-map n Y' Z f' (cube-map n X Y' g' c)) (cube-map n X Z (λ x → f' (g' x)) c) (cube-comp n X Y' Z f' g' c))
papp-lit-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-lit sk X o l (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-lit-deg sk X o l G =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X)
                 (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
                  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))) G)
    (diag-deg sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X G)
    (pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
       (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
       (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
       (λ i → diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) (degen-l X) G i))
       (diag-deg sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X G))
    (snd l)
-- (the connections composed with the degeneracy are the double degeneracy, which is the newer
-- skeleton's degeneracy of the degenerate cube: cube-comp2 at a judgmental pointwise equation)
papp-conj-from-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l lnil G = papp-lit-deg sk X o l G
papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l (lcons m ms) G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
    (papp-lit sk X o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))))
    (papp-lit sk X o l (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
    (λ i → papp-lit sk X o l
       (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X (Line X) (degen-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
          (λ j → papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms
             (cube-comp2 (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) (degen-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (degen-l X) G
                (λ k → cube-map (dims sk) X (Line (Line X)) (λ x → degen-l (Line X) (degen-l X x)) G) j))
          (papp-conj-from-deg (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) i))
    (papp-lit-deg sk X o l G)
papp-conj-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-conj sk X o c (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-conj-deg sk X o lnil G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face1-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
    (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
    (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face1-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G)
papp-conj-deg sk X o (lcons l ls) G = papp-conj-from-deg sk X o l ls G
papp-dnf-from-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (o : Word) (c : Conj) (ds : DNF) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-dnf-from sk X o c ds (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-dnf-from-deg sk X o c lnil G = papp-conj-deg sk X o c G
papp-dnf-from-deg sk X o c (lcons d ds) G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X)
    (papp-conj sk X o c (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
       (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))))
    (papp-conj sk X o c (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
    (λ i → papp-conj sk X o c
       (pcat (Cube (dims sk) (Line X))
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-map (suc (dims sk)) X (Line X) (degen-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)))
          (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)
          (λ j → papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds
             (cube-comp2 (dims sk) X (Line X) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) (degen-l X) (line-map X (Line X) (degen-l X)) (degen-l X) G
                (λ k → cube-map (dims sk) X (Line (Line X)) (λ x → degen-l (Line X) (degen-l X x)) G) j))
          (papp-dnf-from-deg (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) d ds (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) i))
    (papp-conj-deg sk X o c G)
papp-deg : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (f : DNF) (G : Cube (dims sk) X) →
  PathP (λ i → Cube (dims sk) X) (papp-cube sk X f (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G)) G
papp-deg sk X lnil G =
  pcat (Cube (dims sk) X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) (cube-map (dims sk) X (Line X) (degen-l X) G))
    (cube-map (dims sk) X X (λ x → x) G) G
    (cube-comp (dims sk) X (Line X) X (face0-l X) (degen-l X) G) (cube-id (dims sk) X G)
papp-deg sk X (lcons c cs) G = papp-dnf-from-deg sk X #0 c cs G
-- path application on cubes over cubes: the same composite of generators as papp-cube, on the fibres
-- over the base's image (the case on a variable index is the dependent eliminator, since the base's
-- image is computed by the same case)
diag-sk-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (diag-sk sk k X c)
diag-sk-d lnil k X F c d = face0-o X F c d
diag-sk-d (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X F c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F c d) (weq k #0)
diag-sk-d (lcons e-dim sk) k X F c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F
                 (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                  else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
    (weq k #0)
papp-lit-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-lit sk X o l c)
papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F
                 (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c
                  else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F c d)
    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d))
    (snd l)
papp-conj-from-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c)
papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l lnil c d = papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d
papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l (lcons m ms) c d =
  papp-lit-d sk X F o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
    (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))
papp-conj-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-conj sk X o cj c)
papp-conj-d sk X F o lnil c d = dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face1-l X) (face1-o X F) c d
papp-conj-d sk X F o (lcons l ls) c d = papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l ls c d
papp-dnf-from-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (ds : DNF) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c)
papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj lnil c d = papp-conj-d sk X F o cj c d
papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj (lcons e es) c d =
  papp-conj-d sk X F o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
    (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))
papp-cube-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (f : DNF) (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) →
  DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c → DCube (dims sk) X F (papp-cube sk X f c)
papp-cube-d sk X F lnil c d = dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d
papp-cube-d sk X F (lcons cj cs) c d = papp-dnf-from-d sk X F #0 cj cs c d

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6a: contexts and meanings over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A context over a skeleton is a cube of the skeleton's contexts, one direction per
-- dimension entry; a meaning over it with values in Z is a cube over that cube of maps from each
-- vertex's environments into Z. A term's values are TV s, a semantic type of shape s with an element.
CtxV : Lst Entry → Type 1
CtxV sk = fst (CtxE sk)
EnvV : (sk : Lst Entry) → CtxV sk → Type 1
EnvV sk γ = snd (CtxE sk) γ
FbE : (sk : Lst Entry) (Z : Type 1) → CtxV sk → Type 1
FbE sk Z γ = EnvV sk γ → Z
CCtx : Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
CCtx = (ccsk : Lst Entry) × Cube (dims ccsk) (CtxV ccsk)
Mean : CCtx → Type 1 → Type 1
Mean Γ Z = DCube (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (snd Γ)
fmapM : (Γ : CCtx) (Z Z' : Type 1) → (Z → Z') → Mean Γ Z → Mean Γ Z'
fmapM Γ Z Z' h M = dcube-fmap (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (fst Γ) Z') (λ γ e ρ → h (e ρ)) (snd Γ) M
TV : TyShape → Type 1
-- binder names chosen not to collide: t46
TV s = (tvA : Sem s) × El s tvA
-- Γ extended by a type that a meaning M over Γ gives at each vertex (f reads the type off M's value;
-- a λ's body's context is this at the λ's own conclusion, so no path is needed between them)
extM : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) (Y : Type 1) (f : (γ : CtxV (fst Γ)) → (EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Y) → EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Sem a) → Mean Γ Y → CCtx
extM Γ a Y f M =
  (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ) ,
   dcube-map (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Y) (CtxV (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ))) (λ γ e → (γ , f γ e)) (snd Γ) M)
-- Γ extended by a dimension: its cube degenerate in the new (newest) direction
dext : CCtx → CCtx
dext Γ = (lcons e-dim (fst Γ) , cube-map (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (Line (CtxV (fst Γ))) (degen-l (CtxV (fst Γ))) (snd Γ))
-- weakening a meaning to the extended contexts
wkM : (Γ : CCtx) (a : TyShape) (Y : Type 1) (f : (γ : CtxV (fst Γ)) → (EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Y) → EnvV (fst Γ) γ → Sem a) (M : Mean Γ Y)
  (Z : Type 1) → Mean Γ Z → Mean (extM Γ a Y f M) Z
wkM Γ a Y f M Z N =
  dcube-push (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (CtxV (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) Y) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (FbE (lcons (e-ty a) (fst Γ)) Z)
    (λ γ e → (γ , f γ e)) (λ γ e N' ρ → N' (fst ρ)) (snd Γ) M N
dwkM : (Γ : CCtx) (Z : Type 1) → Mean Γ Z → Mean (dext Γ) Z
dwkM Γ Z N =
  dcube-reidx (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (Line (CtxV (fst Γ))) (FbE (fst Γ) Z) (LineO (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z))
    (degen-l (CtxV (fst Γ))) (degen-o (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) Z)) (snd Γ) N

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6c: variables over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) A variable of a skeleton: one of its term entries, by recursion on the skeleton (none:
-- the newest entry; some: one below it; a dimension entry is skipped). Its code's de Bruijn index
-- counts every entry; its shape and its meaning (a projection out of each vertex's environment) are
-- computed from it, so a variable judgment's meaning is the cube of that projection over the context.
VarP : Lst Entry → Type
VarP lnil = Empty
VarP (lcons e-dim sk) = VarP sk
VarP (lcons (e-ty a) sk) = Opt (VarP sk)
var-shape : (sk : Lst Entry) → VarP sk → TyShape
var-shape lnil v = Empty-rec v
var-shape (lcons e-dim sk) v = var-shape sk v
var-shape (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none = a
var-shape (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) = var-shape sk v
var-word : (sk : Lst Entry) → VarP sk → Word
var-word lnil v = Empty-rec v
var-word (lcons e-dim sk) v = %wsucc (var-word sk v)
var-word (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none = #0
var-word (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) = %wsucc (var-word sk v)
varM : (sk : Lst Entry) (v : VarP sk) (γ : CtxV sk) → EnvV sk γ → TV (var-shape sk v)
varM lnil v γ ρ = Empty-rec v
varM (lcons e-dim sk) v γ ρ = varM sk v γ ρ
varM (lcons (e-ty a) sk) none γ ρ = (snd γ (fst ρ) , snd ρ)
varM (lcons (e-ty a) sk) (some v) γ ρ = varM sk v (fst γ) (fst ρ)
varCube : (Γ : CCtx) (v : VarP (fst Γ)) → Mean Γ (TV (var-shape (fst Γ) v))
varCube Γ v = dcube-of (dims (fst Γ)) (CtxV (fst Γ)) (FbE (fst Γ) (TV (var-shape (fst Γ) v))) (varM (fst Γ) v) (snd Γ)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- P2.6b: naturality of the maps of cubes over cubes
-- (2026-11-12) Composites of the structural maps agree with the map of the composite: paths, by
-- induction on the dimension (each line version composes judgmentally).
fmap-fmap : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' F2 : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (h' : (x : X) → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F2 c) (dcube-fmap n X F' F2 h' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d)) (dcube-fmap n X F F2 (λ x y → h' x (h x y)) c d)
fmap-fmap zero X F F' F2 h h' c d = λ i → h' c (h c d)
fmap-fmap (suc n) X F F' F2 h h' c d =
  fmap-fmap n (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F2) (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap X F' F2 h') c d
fmap-reidx : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (F' F2 : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X') (g : (x : X) → F x → F' (f x))
  (h : (x : X') → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F2 (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' F' F2 h (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F' f g c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F2 f (λ x y → h (f x) (g x y)) c d)
fmap-reidx zero X X' F F' F2 f g h c d = λ i → h (f c) (g c d)
fmap-reidx (suc n) X X' F F' F2 f g h c d =
  fmap-reidx n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (LineO X' F2) (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F F' f g) (lineo-fmap X' F' F2 h) c d
reidx-fmap : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x) (f : X → X')
  (g : (x : X) → F2 x → F' (f x)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F2 F' f g c (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F F' f (λ x y → g x (h x y)) c d)
reidx-fmap zero X X' F F2 F' h f g c d = λ i → g c (h c d)
reidx-fmap (suc n) X X' F F2 F' h f g c d =
  reidx-fmap n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-fmap X F F2 h) (line-map X X' f) (lineo-reidx X X' F2 F' f g) c d
fmap-push : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F : X → Type 1) (F' F2 : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X')
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F x → F' (f x y)) (h : (x : X') → F' x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F2 (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d))
    (dcube-fmap n X' F' F2 h (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d) (dcube-push n X X' Y F F' f g c d e))
    (dcube-push n X X' Y F F2 f (λ x y z → h (f x y) (g x y z)) c d e)
fmap-push zero X X' Y F F' F2 f g h c d e = λ i → h (f c d) (g c d e)
fmap-push (suc n) X X' Y F F' F2 f g h c d e =
  fmap-push n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X' F') (LineO X' F2) (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-push X X' Y F F' f g)
    (lineo-fmap X' F' F2 h) c d e
push-fmap : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X') (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x)
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F2 x → F' (f x y)) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d))
    (dcube-push n X X' Y F2 F' f g c d (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c e)) (dcube-push n X X' Y F F' f (λ x y z → g x y (h x z)) c d e)
push-fmap zero X X' Y F F2 F' f h g c d e = λ i → g c d (h c e)
push-fmap (suc n) X X' Y F F2 F' f h g c d e =
  push-fmap n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-fmap X F F2 h)
    (lineo-push X X' Y F2 F' f g) c d e
fmap-pull : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (Y F F2 : X → Type 1) (F' : X' → Type 1) (f : (x : X) → Y x → X')
  (g : (x : X) (y : Y x) → F' (f x y) → F x) (h : (x : X) → F x → F2 x) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X Y c) (e : DCube n X' F' (dcube-map n X Y X' f c d)) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X F2 c)
    (dcube-fmap n X F F2 h c (dcube-pull n X X' Y F F' f g c d e)) (dcube-pull n X X' Y F2 F' f (λ x y z → h x (g x y z)) c d e)
fmap-pull zero X X' Y F F2 F' f g h c d e = λ i → h c (g c d e)
fmap-pull (suc n) X X' Y F F2 F' f g h c d e =
  fmap-pull n (Line X) (Line X') (LineO X Y) (LineO X F) (LineO X F2) (LineO X' F') (lineo-map X Y X' f) (lineo-pull X X' Y F F' f g)
    (lineo-fmap X F F2 h) c d e
-- a fibrewise map commutes with carrying a cube over a base along a path of bases (by the filler of
-- the transport)
fmap-transp : (n : Nat) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (c0 c1 : Cube n X) (p : PathP (λ i → Cube n X) c0 c1)
  (d : DCube n X F c0) →
  PathP (λ j → DCube n X F' c1)
    (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c1 (comp (λ i → DCube n X F (p i)) (λ i → []) d))
    (comp (λ i → DCube n X F' (p i)) (λ i → []) (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c0 d))
fmap-transp n X F F' h c0 c1 p d =
  λ j → comp (λ i → DCube n X F' (p i))
    (λ i → [ j = 0 ↦ dcube-fmap n X F F' h (p i) (comp (λ k → DCube n X F (p (i ∧ k))) (λ k → [ i = 0 ↦ d ]) d) ])
    (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c0 d)
-- (2026-11-12) a fibrewise map commutes with reindexing along a map of the base whose fibre maps
-- commute with it pointwise (q, judgmental at each generator below: refl)
fmap-gen : (n : Nat) (X X' : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (G G' : X' → Type 1) (f : X → X')
  (g : (x : X) → F x → G (f x)) (g' : (x : X) → F' x → G' (f x)) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (h2 : (x : X') → G x → G' x)
  (q : PathP (λ i → (x : X) → F x → G' (f x)) (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) (λ x y → g' x (h x y))) (c : Cube n X) (d : DCube n X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' G G' h2 (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G f g c d))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
fmap-gen n X X' F F' G G' f g g' h h2 q c d =
  pcat (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
    (dcube-fmap n X' G G' h2 (cube-map n X X' f c) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G f g c d))
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) c d)
    (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-reidx n X X' F G G' f g h2 c d)
    (pcat (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → h2 (f x) (g x y)) c d)
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → g' x (h x y)) c d)
       (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d))
       (λ i → dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (q i) c d)
       (psym (DCube n X' G' (cube-map n X X' f c))
          (dcube-reidx n X X' F' G' f g' c (dcube-fmap n X F F' h c d)) (dcube-reidx n X X' F G' f (λ x y → g' x (h x y)) c d)
          (reidx-fmap n X X' F F' G' h f g' c d)))
-- a fibrewise map commutes with path application on cubes over cubes (by the recursion of
-- papp-cube-d, each generator by fmap-gen)
fmap-diag-sk : (sk : Lst Entry) (k : Word) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (diag-sk sk k X c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (diag-sk sk k X c) (diag-sk-d sk k X F c d))
    (diag-sk-d sk k X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-diag-sk lnil k X F F' h c d = λ i → h (fst c) (fst d)
fmap-diag-sk (lcons (e-ty s) sk) k X F F' h c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                 (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c)
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) F (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F c d) b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F' (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) X (face0-l X) c else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X c))
                    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F') F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)) b))
    (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) (face0-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
       (λ i L D → h (fst L) (fst D)) c d)
    (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) X F F' h c d) (weq k #0)
fmap-diag-sk (lcons e-dim sk) k X F F' h c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F'
                    (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                     else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                 (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h
                    (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                     else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F
                                   (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                                    else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
                          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
                       b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F'
                                (if b then cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) c
                                 else diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
                    (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO X F') (diag-l X) (diag-o X F') c
                       (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F') c
                          (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d)))
                    b))
    (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO X F) (LineO X F')
       (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) (diag-o X F') (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)) (lineo-fmap X F F' h)
       (λ i Q D → lineo-fmap X F F' h (diag-l X Q) (diag-o X F Q D)) c d)
    (pcat (DCube (dims sk) (Line X) (LineO X F') (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)))
       (dcube-fmap (dims sk) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)
          (diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c))
          (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F') c
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h c d)))
       (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) c d))
       (λ i → diag-sk-d sk (%wsub k #1) (Line X) (LineO X F') (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (exch-l X) c)
          (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
             (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (exch-l X) (exch-o X F) (exch-o X F')
             (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h)) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
             (λ j Q D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (exch-l X Q) (exch-o X F Q D)) c d i)))
    (weq k #0)
fmap-papp-lit : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (l : Lit)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-lit sk X o l c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-lit sk X o l c) (papp-lit-d sk X F o l c d))
    (papp-lit-d sk X F' o l c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l c d =
  bool-elim1 (λ b → PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F'
                    (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                 (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F'  h
                    (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c))
                    (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F
                                   (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F c d)
                       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
                          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)) b))
                 (bool-elim1 (λ b → DCube (dims sk) X F'
                                (if b then diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X c else diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
                    (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
                       (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F') (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))) b))
    (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F F' h c d)
    (pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)))
       (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c))
          (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d)))
       (diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F') (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F') c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
       (fmap-diag-sk sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F) (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) c d))
       (λ i → diag-sk-d sk (%wadd (fst l) o) X F' (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (rev-l X) c)
          (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (rev-l X) (rev-o X F) (rev-o X F')
             (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (λ j L D → lineo-fmap X F F' h (rev-l X L) (rev-o X F L D)) c d i)))
    (snd l)
fmap-papp-conj-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (l : Lit) (ms : Conj)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj-from sk X o l ms c) (papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l ms c d))
    (papp-conj-from-d sk X F' o l ms c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l lnil c d = fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l c d
fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l (lcons m ms) c d =
  pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj-from sk X o l (lcons m ms) c) (papp-conj-from-d sk X F o l (lcons m ms) c d))
    (papp-lit-d sk X F' o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))))
    (papp-conj-from-d sk X F' o l (lcons m ms) c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-papp-lit sk X F F' h o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
    (λ i → papp-lit-d sk X F' o l (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
       (pcat (DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F' (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)))
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c))
             (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F') c
                (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
          (fmap-papp-conj-from (lcons e-dim sk) X F F' h (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) c d))
          (λ j → papp-conj-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) m ms (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (meet-l X) c)
             (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
                (meet-l X) (meet-o X F) (meet-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
                (λ k L D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (meet-l X L) (meet-o X F L D)) c d j)) i))
fmap-papp-conj : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (cj : Conj)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-conj sk X o cj c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-conj sk X o cj c) (papp-conj-d sk X F o cj c d))
    (papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o lnil c d =
  fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face1-l X) (face1-o X F) (face1-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
    (λ i L D → h (fst (snd L)) (fst (snd D))) c d
fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o (lcons l ls) c d = fmap-papp-conj-from sk X F F' h o l ls c d
fmap-papp-dnf-from : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (o : Word) (cj : Conj) (ds : DNF)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj ds c) (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj ds c d))
    (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F' o cj ds c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h o cj lnil c d = fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o cj c d
fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h o cj (lcons e es) c d =
  pcat (DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj (lcons e es) c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from sk X o cj (lcons e es) c) (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F o cj (lcons e es) c d))
    (papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))))
    (papp-dnf-from-d sk X F' o cj (lcons e es) c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
    (fmap-papp-conj sk X F F' h o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
          (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
    (λ i → papp-conj-d sk X F' o cj (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
       (pcat (DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F' (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)))
          (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h (papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c))
             (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-fmap (suc (suc (dims sk))) X F F' h (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
                (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d)))
          (papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F')) (join-l X) (join-o X F') c
                (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d)))
          (fmap-papp-dnf-from (lcons e-dim sk) X F F' h (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (join-l X) (join-o X F) c d))
          (λ j → papp-dnf-from-d (lcons e-dim sk) X F' (%wsucc o) e es (cube-map (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (join-l X) c)
             (fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) (Line (Line X)) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F'))
                (join-l X) (join-o X F) (join-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h))
                (λ k L D → lineo-fmap (Line X) (LineO X F) (LineO X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) (join-l X L) (join-o X F L D)) c d j)) i))
fmap-papp : (sk : Lst Entry) (X : Type 1) (F F' : X → Type 1) (h : (x : X) → F x → F' x) (f : DNF)
  (c : Cube (suc (dims sk)) X) (d : DCube (suc (dims sk)) X F c) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F' (papp-cube sk X f c))
    (dcube-fmap (dims sk) X F F' h (papp-cube sk X f c) (papp-cube-d sk X F f c d))
    (papp-cube-d sk X F' f c (dcube-fmap (suc (dims sk)) X F F' h c d))
fmap-papp sk X F F' h lnil c d =
  fmap-gen (dims sk) (Line X) X (LineO X F) (LineO X F') F F' (face0-l X) (face0-o X F) (face0-o X F') (lineo-fmap X F F' h) h
    (λ i L D → h (fst L) (fst D)) c d
fmap-papp sk X F F' h (lcons cj cs) c d = fmap-papp-dnf-from sk X F F' h #0 cj cs c d
